This extension adds AC Unity modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]Epic[/*]
[*]Ubisoft Connect[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Installs AnvilToolkit itself, recognised by an "anviltoolkit.exe" file.[/*]
[*]Installs mods with a file or folder named one of: "dlc_10" or "dlc_11" to the game folder itself (no subfolder).[/*]
[*]Installs mods with an "Extracted" folder to the game folder itself (no subfolder).[/*]
[*]Forgefolder mods are installed to the game folder itself (no subfolder).[/*]
[*]Datafolder mods are installed to the game folder itself (no subfolder).[/*]
[*]Installs mods with a ".data" file to the game folder itself (no subfolder).[/*]
[*]Installs mods with a file or folder named one of: "version.dll" or "ACUFixes" to the game folder itself (no subfolder).[/*]
[*]Installs mods with a file or folder named one of: "d3d11.dll" to the game folder itself (no subfolder).[/*]
[*]Installs mods with a ".forge" file to the game folder itself (no subfolder).[/*]
[*]Installs mods with a "videos" folder to the game folder itself (no subfolder).[/*]
[*]Installs mods with a file with the ".dds" extension to the "ResoRep\modded" folder.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[/list]

